2025-05-01 03:30:48 - Thread-1471 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage
• Match.id : primary key to identify each match (optional in the analysis)  
• Match.home_team_goal / Match.away_team_goal : decide the outcome (home win / draw / away win)  
• Match.home_player_1 … Match.home_player_11 : players who actually played for the home side (NULL ⇒ did not play → must be excluded)  
• Match.away_player_1 … Match.away_player_11 : players who actually played for the away side (NULL ⇒ did not play → must be excluded)  
• Player.player_api_id : joins the numeric id stored in the Match‑table columns to the Player table  
• Player.player_name : human–readable name of the player (for the final answer)  

Main conditions to be applied
1. Ignore matches that end in a draw → home_team_goal ≠ away_team_goal  
2. A player is counted only if his id appears in one of the 22 positional columns and is NOT NULL  
3. For each non‑draw match
   • if home_team_goal  >  away_team_goal  → every non‑NULL home_player_* counts one win, every non‑NULL away_player_* counts one loss  
   • if home_team_goal  <  away_team_goal  → every non‑NULL away_player_* counts one win, every non‑NULL home_player_* counts one loss  

10 exploratory → step‑by‑step SQL queries
Each query is limited to 20 rows so that you can inspect interim data.  
(Remember to execute them one at a time.)

```sql
-- 1. Peek at some goal data to understand the outcome field
SELECT id, home_team_goal, away_team_goal
FROM "Match"
WHERE home_team_goal IS NOT NULL AND away_team_goal IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect one positional column to see raw player ids
SELECT DISTINCT "home_player_1"
FROM "Match"
WHERE "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show a handful of player ids together with the final score for non‑draw matches
SELECT id, home_team_goal, away_team_goal,
       "home_player_1", "away_player_1"
FROM "Match"
WHERE home_team_goal <> away_team_goal
  AND "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
  AND "away_player_1" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. List the 20 most‑frequent ids appearing in any home position
SELECT player_id, COUNT(*) AS freq
FROM (
      SELECT "home_player_1" AS player_id FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_2" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_2" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_3" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_3" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_4" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_4" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_5" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_5" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_6" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_6" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_7" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_7" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_8" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_8" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_9" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_9" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_10" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_10" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL
      SELECT "home_player_11" FROM "Match" WHERE "home_player_11" IS NOT NULL
) AS t
GROUP BY player_id
ORDER BY freq DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Build the set of all winners (home side only) – preliminary 20 rows
SELECT m.id, m.home_team_goal, m.away_team_goal,
       hp.player_id
FROM (
        SELECT id,
               home_team_goal, away_team_goal,
               "home_player_1" AS player_id FROM "Match"
        WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal
              AND "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
        UNION ALL
        SELECT id, home_team_goal, away_team_goal, "home_player_2" FROM "Match"
        WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal
              AND "home_player_2" IS NOT NULL
        -- repeat for the remaining 9 home positions …
) AS hp
JOIN "Match" AS m  ON m.id = hp.id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same idea but for winners on the away side
SELECT m.id, m.home_team_goal, m.away_team_goal,
       ap.player_id
FROM (
        SELECT id,
               home_team_goal, away_team_goal,
               "away_player_1" AS player_id FROM "Match"
        WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal
              AND "away_player_1" IS NOT NULL
        UNION ALL
        SELECT id, home_team_goal, away_team_goal, "away_player_2" FROM "Match"
        WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal
              AND "away_player_2" IS NOT NULL
        -- repeat for the remaining 9 away positions …
) AS ap
JOIN "Match" AS m  ON m.id = ap.id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Combine home‑win and away‑win sets, count total wins per player
SELECT player_id, COUNT(*) AS win_cnt
FROM (
      -- home‑side winners
      SELECT "home_player_1" AS player_id FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_2" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_2" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_3" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_3" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_4" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_4" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_5" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_5" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_6" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_6" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_7" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_7" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_8" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_8" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_9" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_9" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_10" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_10" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_11" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal > away_team_goal AND "home_player_11" IS NOT NULL
      -- away‑side winners
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_1" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_1" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_2" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_2" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_3" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_3" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_4" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_4" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_5" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_5" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_6" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_6" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_7" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_7" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_8" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_8" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_9" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_9" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_10" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_10" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_11" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal > home_team_goal AND "away_player_11" IS NOT NULL
) AS winners
GROUP BY player_id
ORDER BY win_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Repeat the same pattern for losses (swap the goal comparison)
SELECT player_id, COUNT(*) AS loss_cnt
FROM (
      -- home‑side losers
      SELECT "home_player_1" AS player_id FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal < away_team_goal AND "home_player_1" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "home_player_2" FROM "Match"
      WHERE home_team_goal < away_team_goal AND "home_player_2" IS NOT NULL
      -- … repeat for 3‑11
      -- away‑side losers
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_1" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal < home_team_goal AND "away_player_1" IS NOT NULL
      UNION ALL  SELECT "away_player_2" FROM "Match"
      WHERE away_team_goal < home_team_goal AND "away_player_2" IS NOT NULL
      -- … repeat for 3‑11
) AS losers
GROUP BY player_id
ORDER BY loss_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Attach player names to the TOP winning players
WITH win_totals AS (
  SELECT player_id, COUNT(*) AS win_cnt
  FROM (
        -- use exactly the same UNION ALL block from query #7
  ) AS winners
  GROUP BY player_id
)
SELECT p.player_name, w.win_cnt
FROM win_totals AS w
JOIN "Player"   AS p ON p.player_api_id = w.player_id
ORDER BY w.win_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL: one row for the all‑time most wins and one row for the all‑time most losses
WITH win_totals AS (
  SELECT player_id, COUNT(*) AS win_cnt
  FROM (
        -- (same UNION ALL as in #7) 
  ) GROUP BY player_id
),
loss_totals AS (
  SELECT player_id, COUNT(*) AS loss_cnt
  FROM (
        -- (same UNION ALL as in #8)
  ) GROUP BY player_id
),
max_win AS (
  SELECT player_id, win_cnt
  FROM win_totals
  ORDER BY win_cnt DESC
  LIMIT 1
),
max_loss AS (
  SELECT player_id, loss_cnt
  FROM loss_totals
  ORDER BY loss_cnt DESC
  LIMIT 1
)
SELECT 'Most wins'  AS category, p1.player_name, mw.win_cnt  AS matches
FROM max_win AS mw
JOIN "Player" AS p1 ON p1.player_api_id = mw.player_id
UNION ALL
SELECT 'Most losses', p2.player_name, ml.loss_cnt
FROM max_loss AS ml
JOIN "Player" AS p2 ON p2.player_api_id = ml.player_id
LIMIT 20;
```

Run the sequence above (filling in the “repeat …” blocks with the remaining 9 positional columns each time) and the last query (#10) will give you:

• the player who appeared in the highest number of winning matches  
• the player who appeared in the highest number of losing matches  

both restricted to matches where they actually played and excluding all draws.
